---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const weaponJourneyItems = [
  { title: "Part I - Astras", href: "/astras/part-1", eyebrow: "Mantra weapons", description: "Weapons invoked through mantra, concentration, discipline, and divine authority.", status: "available" },
  { title: "Part II - Ayudhas", href: "/astras/part-2", eyebrow: "Divine weapons", description: "The eternal weapons carried by the gods, inseparable from their divine identities.", status: "available" },
  { title: "Part III - Epic Weapons", href: "/astras/part-3", eyebrow: "Hero weapons", description: "The legendary weapons of epic heroes, including Gandiva, Kodanda, Vijaya, and Chandrahasa.", status: "available" },
];

const weaponGroups = [
  {
    number: "01",
    title: "Divine Bows",
    note: "The most celebrated bows of the epics, each carrying a unique legacy of valor and Dharma.",
    columns: ["Weapon", "Hero", "Bestowed By / Origin"],
    rows: [
      ["Kodanda", "Rama", "Traditional bow of Rama"],
      ["Gandiva", "Arjuna", "Agni, originally from Brahma through Varuna"],
      ["Vijaya", "Karna", "Given to Parashurama; traditionally associated with Vishvakarma's craftsmanship"],
      ["Shiva Dhanush (Pinaka in the Ramayana tradition)", "Broken by Rama at Sita's svayamvara", "Shiva"],
    ],
  },
  {
    number: "02",
    title: "Legendary Swords",
    note: "Symbols of courage, kingship, and righteous warfare.",
    columns: ["Weapon", "Hero", "Origin"],
    rows: [
      ["Chandrahasa", "Ravana", "Gift from Shiva"],
      ["Asi (in heroic traditions)", "Various kings and warriors", "Primordial sword originating from Brahma"],
    ],
  },
  {
    number: "03",
    title: "Divine Axes",
    note: "Weapons associated with unmatched martial mastery.",
    columns: ["Weapon", "Hero", "Origin"],
    rows: [["Parashu", "Parashurama", "Gift of Shiva"]],
  },
  {
    number: "04",
    title: "Maces and Blunt Weapons",
    note: "Weapons that relied on immense strength, discipline, and mastery of close combat.",
    columns: ["Weapon", "Hero", "Origin"],
    rows: [
      ["Gada", "Bhima", "Mastered under Balarama"],
      ["Gada", "Duryodhana", "Mastered under Balarama"],
      ["Gada", "Hanuman", "Symbol of divine strength and devotion"],
    ],
  },
  {
    number: "05",
    title: "Spears, Lances and Special Weapons",
    note: "Rare weapons bestowed for decisive moments in battle.",
    columns: ["Weapon", "Hero", "Origin"],
    rows: [
      ["Vasavi Shakti", "Karna", "Gift from Indra in exchange for his divine armor and earrings"],
      ["Shakti Spear", "Indrajit", "Divine boon described in Ramayana traditions"],
    ],
  },
  {
    number: "06",
    title: "Sacred Objects and Heroic Implements",
    note: "Some heroes are remembered not only for weapons but also for sacred objects inseparably linked to their deeds.",
    columns: ["Object", "Hero", "Significance"],
    rows: [
      ["Mountain-bearing Strength", "Hanuman", "Carrying the Sanjeevani mountain"],
      ["Mace (Gada)", "Hanuman", "Symbol of unwavering devotion and immense power"],
    ],
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Part III - Legendary Weapons | Sanatana Path" description="A dedicated atlas page for the legendary weapons of epic heroes, including Kodanda, Gandiva, Vijaya, Chandrahasa, and more." image="/images/home/home-astras.webp" type="article">
  <article class="weapon-page">
    <section class="weapon-hero">
      <div class="hero-glass">
        <a class="back-link" href="/astras">Weapons overview</a>
        <p class="eyebrow">Atlas of Divine Weapons</p>
        <h1>Part III - Epic Weapons</h1>
        <strong>Legendary Weapons of the Epic Heroes</strong>
        <p>Not every legendary weapon described in the Hindu epics is an Astra or an Ayudha. Some became sacred through the courage, destiny, and Dharma of the heroes who carried them.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <nav class="weapon-progress" aria-label="Sacred weapons part navigation">
      <div class="progress-head"><span>Part path</span><strong>Sacred Weapons</strong></div>
      <div>{weaponJourneyItems.map((item, index) => <a href={item.href} class="progress-item" title={item.description}><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span><strong>{item.title}</strong><small>{item.eyebrow}</small></a>)}</div>
    </nav>

    <div class="weapon-layout">
      <main class="weapon-groups">
        <section class="intro-panel"><p>Some are extraordinary bows, swords, maces, spears, and other sacred weapons bestowed upon great heroes by gods, celestial beings, or revered sages.</p><p>Though not usually invoked through mantras like Astras, nor counted among the eternal Ayudhas of the gods, they remain some of the most celebrated weapons in Hindu sacred literature.</p></section>
        {weaponGroups.map((group) => (
          <section class="weapon-group"><header><span>{group.number}</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Epic weapon category</p><h2>{group.title}</h2><p>{group.note}</p></div></header><div class="weapon-table" role="table" aria-label={group.title}><div class="table-row table-head" role="row">{group.columns.map((column) => <span role="columnheader">{column}</span>)}</div>{group.rows.map((row) => <div class="table-row" role="row">{row.map((cell) => <span role="cell">{cell}</span>)}</div>)}</div></section>
        ))}
        <section class="intro-panel"><p>These legendary weapons are remembered not because of the destruction they caused, but because of the heroes who wielded them.</p><p>The Kodanda evokes the unwavering righteousness of Rama. The Gandiva became a symbol of Arjuna's duty on the battlefield of Kurukshetra. The Vijaya reflected Karna's unmatched skill and determination. The Chandrahasa stood as a mark of Shiva's favor toward Ravana.</p><p>Each weapon tells the story of its bearer, reminding us that true greatness lies not in the weapon itself, but in the character of the one who wields it.</p></section>
      </main>
      <aside class="next-panel"><p class="eyebrow">The journey continues</p><h2>The Complete Atlas</h2><p>With Astras, Ayudhas, and the legendary weapons of the epic heroes now before us, the deeper exploration can begin.</p><p>Each chapter can uncover the origin, powers, scriptural references, notable wielders, famous battles, and enduring significance of these extraordinary weapons.</p><a href="/astras">Back to overview</a></aside>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :global(body:has(.weapon-page)){background:#020d13;color:#fff4df}:global(body:has(.weapon-page)::before){display:none}.weapon-page{min-height:100svh;padding-bottom:4rem;background:radial-gradient(circle at 78% 0%,rgb(255 122 79/.14),transparent 28rem),linear-gradient(180deg,#020d13,#031519 54%,#020d13)}.weapon-hero{position:relative;width:min(1460px,calc(100% - 2rem));min-height:clamp(27rem,54svh,36rem);margin:1.25rem auto 0;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid rgb(255 122 79/.32);border-radius:1.15rem;background-image:linear-gradient(90deg,rgb(2 13 19/.92),rgb(2 13 19/.44) 46%,rgb(2 13 19/.12)),url("/images/home/home-astras.webp");background-position:center,right center;background-size:auto,auto 100%;background-repeat:no-repeat;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.025),0 28px 90px rgb(0 0 0/.3)}.weapon-hero::after{position:absolute;inset:0;background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgb(2 13 19/.28),transparent 20%,transparent 74%,rgb(2 13 19/.32));content:"";pointer-events:none}.hero-glass{position:relative;z-index:1;width:min(43rem,45%);margin:clamp(1.4rem,3vw,2.7rem);border:1px solid rgb(255 122 79/.38);border-radius:1rem;padding:clamp(1.25rem,2.6vw,2rem);background:linear-gradient(145deg,rgb(3 13 20/.58),rgb(3 13 20/.26)),radial-gradient(circle at 16% 0%,rgb(255 122 79/.18),transparent 52%);box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.08),0 24px 75px rgb(0 0 0/.22);backdrop-filter:blur(22px) saturate(126%)}.back-link{display:inline-flex;width:fit-content;margin-bottom:clamp(1rem,2vw,1.5rem);border:1px solid rgb(255 122 79/.34);border-radius:999px;padding:.5rem .72rem;background:rgb(3 13 20/.38);color:#ff9b7d;font-size:.72rem;font-weight:850;text-decoration:none;backdrop-filter:blur(14px)}.eyebrow{margin:0 0 .6rem;color:#ff9b7d;font-size:.7rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase}h1,h2{margin:0;color:#fff4df;font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0;line-height:.98}.hero-glass h1{font-size:clamp(3rem,5vw,5.4rem)}.hero-glass strong{display:block;margin-top:.65rem;color:#ffd3bf;font-size:clamp(1.05rem,1.5vw,1.3rem)}.hero-glass p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:44rem;margin:1rem 0 0;color:#eee0ca;font-size:clamp(1rem,1.18vw,1.12rem);line-height:1.75}.weapon-progress{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto minmax(0,1fr);gap:.75rem;align-items:center;width:min(1460px,calc(100% - 2rem));margin:clamp(1rem,2vw,1.35rem) auto 0;border:1px solid rgb(255 122 79/.28);border-radius:1rem;padding:.72rem;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgb(255 122 79/.08),rgb(2 13 19/.48));box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.045),0 16px 38px rgb(0 0 0/.18)}.progress-head{display:grid;min-width:9rem;border-right:1px solid rgb(255 122 79/.22);padding:.15rem .95rem .15rem .35rem}.progress-head span{color:#ff9b7d;font-size:.58rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.13em;text-transform:uppercase}.progress-head strong{margin-top:.12rem;color:#fff4df;font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:500}.weapon-progress>div:last-child{display:flex;gap:.46rem;min-width:0;overflow-x:auto;scrollbar-width:none}.progress-item{display:grid;min-width:10.7rem;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;align-items:center;gap:.12rem .48rem;border:1px solid rgb(255 122 79/.28);border-radius:999px;padding:.48rem .72rem .48rem .46rem;background:rgb(255 122 79/.07);color:#fff4df;text-decoration:none}.progress-item>span{display:grid;width:1.78rem;height:1.78rem;grid-row:1/3;place-items:center;border-radius:50%;background:rgb(255 122 79/.16);color:#ffb194;font-size:.58rem;font-weight:900}.progress-item strong,.progress-item small{overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap}.progress-item strong{font-size:.73rem;font-weight:850}.progress-item small{color:#cfa99b;font-size:.55rem;font-weight:850;text-transform:uppercase}.weapon-layout{display:grid;width:min(1460px,calc(100% - 2rem));grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(18rem,23rem);gap:clamp(1.25rem,3vw,2.5rem);margin:clamp(1.25rem,3vw,2rem) auto 0}.weapon-groups{display:grid;gap:1rem}.weapon-group,.next-panel,.intro-panel{border:1px solid rgb(255 122 79/.25);border-radius:1rem;background:linear-gradient(145deg,rgb(3 13 20/.86),rgb(3 13 20/.62));box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.045),0 20px 60px rgb(0 0 0/.18)}.intro-panel{padding:clamp(1rem,2vw,1.35rem);color:#e8decc;line-height:1.75}.weapon-group{overflow:hidden}.weapon-group header{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:clamp(1rem,2vw,1.35rem)}.weapon-group header>span{display:grid;width:2.7rem;height:2.7rem;place-items:center;border:1px solid rgb(255 122 79/.34);border-radius:50%;color:#ffb194;font-size:.72rem;font-weight:900}.weapon-group h2{font-size:clamp(1.6rem,2.4vw,2.35rem)}.weapon-group header p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:70ch;margin:.65rem 0 0;color:#e8decc;line-height:1.75}.weapon-table{display:grid;border-top:1px solid rgb(255 122 79/.18)}.table-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(10rem,.9fr) minmax(10rem,.8fr) minmax(14rem,1.2fr)}.table-row span{min-width:0;border-right:1px solid rgb(255 122 79/.12);border-bottom:1px solid rgb(255 122 79/.12);padding:.82rem .9rem;color:#e8decc;line-height:1.45}.table-row span:last-child{border-right:0}.table-head span{color:#ffb194;background:rgb(255 122 79/.08);font-size:.64rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase}.next-panel{position:sticky;top:6rem;align-self:start;padding:clamp(1rem,2vw,1.35rem)}.next-panel h2{font-size:clamp(1.75rem,2.5vw,2.45rem)}.next-panel p{color:#e8decc;line-height:1.7}.next-panel a{display:inline-flex;margin-top:.5rem;border:1px solid rgb(255 122 79/.32);border-radius:999px;padding:.46rem .68rem;color:#ffb194;background:rgb(255 122 79/.08);font-size:.68rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;text-decoration:none}@media(max-width:980px){.hero-glass{width:auto;margin-top:clamp(10rem,28svh,16rem)}.weapon-hero{background-size:auto,cover}.weapon-progress,.weapon-layout{grid-template-columns:1fr}.progress-head{border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid rgb(255 122 79/.22);padding-bottom:.6rem}.next-panel{position:static}}@media(max-width:720px){.weapon-page{padding-bottom:6rem}.weapon-hero,.weapon-progress,.weapon-layout{width:min(100% - 1rem,1460px)}.hero-glass{margin:clamp(8rem,24svh,12rem) .75rem .75rem}.weapon-group header{grid-template-columns:1fr}.table-row{grid-template-columns:1fr}.table-head{display:none}.table-row span{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(7rem,.42fr) 1fr;gap:.75rem;border-right:0}.table-row span::before{color:#ffb194;font-size:.62rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;content:"Weapon"}.table-row span:nth-child(2)::before{content:"Hero"}.table-row span:nth-child(3)::before{content:"Origin"}}
</style>